km":15.0,"wind_from_deg":[220.0,231.0]},"packet":{"draft_en":"On January 10, 2024, the Texas state monitor at Channelview Drive Water Tower recorded 10.47 ppb of benzene in the 12:00 a.m. CST hour, against a 7-day median of 0.35 ppb. Wind there came from 231 degrees at 3.7 mph. 40 major permitted facilities lie in the upwind corridor. No matching report was found in the records checked; the search is incomplete. Requested follow-up: confirm whether any facility in this corridor reported a release that hour.","draft_es":"El 10 de enero de 2024, el monitor estatal de Texas en Channelview Drive Water Tower registró 10.47 ppb de benceno en la hora de las 12:00 a. m. CST, frente a una mediana de 7 días de 0.35 ppb. El viento venía de 231 grados a 3.7 mph. Hay 40 instalaciones grandes con permiso en el corredor viento arriba. No se encontró un reporte que coincida en los registros revisados; la búsqueda está incompleta. Seguimiento solicitado: confirmar si alguna instalación en este corredor reportó una emisión a esa hora.","drafted_by":"template (deterministic, no AI)","guard":{"passed":true,"rejected":[]}},"cannot_say":["A matching report is not proof the facility caused every reading; other sources can add to a spike.","'Not yet reported' is not a finding about any facility: Texas requires a report only at or above a reportable quantity, and air readings cannot measure how much was released (30 TAC 101.201).","The upwind corridor comes from wind direction at one monitor (geometry only), not a dispersion model; it cannot tell facilities along the same bearing apart.","Facility coordinates are as published by EPA ECHO and may be approximate.","Only regulator-grade monitors whose data the state publishes are used (including two industry-funded Houston Regional Monitoring sites), never low-cost sensors."],"provenance":[{"file":"backtest/agc_2024_48_201_0069_45201.html","url":"https://www.tceq.texas.gov/cgi-bin/compliance/monops/agc_yearly_summary.pl","params":{"user_year":